{"name":"Ken Masters Red","hex":"#ec2c25","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ken","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Kenyang."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To give birth, conceive, beget, be born; to develop (as a fetus); to nourish, sustain (as life)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ken"},{"term":"masters","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of master"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ellipsis of master's degree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masters"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ken Masters","blocks":[{"text":"Ken Masters  is a character in Capcom's Street Fighter fighting game series. The character was first introduced in the 1987 title Street Fighter as an alternate fighter to Ryu. While Ryu is devoted to testing his power, Ken instead focuses on developing a family with his wife Elisa. Ken becomes a mainstay in the following Street Fighter games. An alternate brainwashed version of him, Violent Ken (暴力的なケン), has also been featured in a few of his appearances. Ken's presence is in several sequels to the Street Fighter series in addition to its related media. He has also made crossover appearances in Namco × Capcom, Project X Zone, and Super Smash Bros."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2f/Ken_Masters_%28SF3_-_Third_Strike%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ken_Masters","wikidata":"Q11020382"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/David_Matranga_%2852814179687%29.jpg/500px-David_Matranga_%2852814179687%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/David_Matranga_%2852814179687%29.jpg/500px-David_Matranga_%2852814179687%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"David Matranga voices Ken in Street Fighter 6.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADavid_Matranga_(52814179687).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ab/KenMastersVdesign.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ab/KenMastersVdesign.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKenMastersVdesign.png"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b0/KenMastersix.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=